+
+Target Paper Keywords:
+<<BEGIN TARGET KEYWORDS>> {target_keywords} <<END TARGET KEYWORDS>>
+
+Neighboring Articles in the Network ({n_neighbors} total):
+{neighbor_lines}
+
+Instructions:
+You are given a target article and exactly {n_neighbors} neighboring article(s) listed above, each described by keywords.
+
+For each of the {n_neighbors} neighboring article(s) listed above:
+1. Clearly state whether this article supports the classification of the Target Article into category '{predicted_label}'.
+
+Use the following format for each neighbor:
+
+Article <ID>:
+Support: YES or NO — Does this article support the classification into '{predicted_label}'?
+
+IMPORTANT: Only analyze the {n_neighbors} article(s) listed above. Do not generate analysis for any other articles. Stop after completing all {n_neighbors} article(s).
+
+Base your reasoning only on the keywords and proximity to the target article.
+
+Start your analysis below:
+"""
+
+    if with_chat_template:
+        prompt = tokenizer.apply_chat_template(
+            [{"role": "system", "content": system_message},
+             {"role": "user", "content": user_content}],
+            tokenize=False, add_generation_prompt=True
+        )
+    else:
+        prompt = system_message + "\n" + user_content
+
+    tokens = tokenizer(prompt, return_tensors="pt", add_special_tokens=False).to(device)
+    return tokens
